-- LINEARITY ---------- errors/linear_used_twice_29.march

The linear value `c` cannot be captured by a closure. [linear_captured]
A closure may be called multiple times, which would violate the exactly-once guarantee.
Pass `c` as a parameter to the closure instead.

10 |     let xs = List.map([1, 2, 3], fn x -> x + close(c))
                                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^



-- LINEARITY ---------- errors/linear_used_twice_29.march

The linear value `c` is used more than once here. [linear_used_twice]
Linear values must be consumed exactly once — they cannot be copied or ignored.

11 |     close(c)
               ^


    `c` was already consumed here, inside a closure that can run more than once (each iteration consumes it):

10 |     let xs = List.map([1, 2, 3], fn x -> x + close(c))
                                                        ^
    run `march --explain linear_used_twice`


